From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Say that the cast's sink is not an output anybody chose

A cast makes a sink to send sound to the receiver, and it has been saying
nothing about itself. What reads a new sink reads it as a new output: the
desktop's audio applet offers it, and the session manager ranks it among the
real ones. Either of them may then make it the default output and write that
down, which is how a machine came to be found whose remembered output was a
cast sink that had not existed for days, with seven more behind it.

Leaving the default alone was meant to end that, and it did end this side of
it: nothing in a cast sets the default any more. The entries kept arriving
anyway, because the deciding was never ours. Reading the state afterwards
shows it plainly - the key that was written is the configured default, which
is written when something sets a default, and the only thing a cast does to a
stream is move it.

So the sink now says what it is at the moment it is made. It is virtual,
because there is no device behind it. Its priorities are zero, which takes it
out of the ranking that picks a default rather than placing it low within
one. Nothing is asked of anybody and no policy is fought; what was missing
was only that this was never said.

diff -ruN a/src/nd-pulseaudio.c b/src/nd-pulseaudio.c
--- a/src/nd-pulseaudio.c
+++ b/src/nd-pulseaudio.c
@@ -311,11 +311,30 @@
   g_debug ("NdPulseaudio: Creating sink for: %s", self->name);
   /* We have reached the list end without being cancelled first.
    * This means no screencast sink exist, and we need to create it. */
+  /* Said at creation, because what reads it reads it then: this is somewhere
+   * sound is being sent for as long as a cast lasts, and not an output
+   * anybody chose. A sink that says nothing looks like a headphone being
+   * plugged in, and whatever elects the default output elects it - the
+   * desktop's own audio applet, or the session manager's priority ranking.
+   * Neither of them is wrong to do so; they were simply never told.
+   *
+   * Being told costs nothing and closes the loop that leaving the default
+   * alone did not: a cast no longer sets the default, and it was still being
+   * made the default, by something else, which then wrote it down. A machine
+   * was found afterwards whose remembered output was a sink that had not
+   * existed for days, with seven more behind it.
+   *
+   * node.virtual says there is no device here. The two priorities take it out
+   * of the ranking that picks a default rather than lowering its place in
+   * one. */
   g_autofree gchar *module_args = g_strdup_printf ("sink_name=" ND_PA_SINK "_%.8s"
                                                    " "
                                                    "rate=48000 "
                                                    "sink_properties=device.class=\"sound\" "
                                                    "device.icon_name=\"network-wireless\" "
+                                                   "node.virtual=true "
+                                                   "priority.session=0 "
+                                                   "priority.driver=0 "
                                                    "device.description=\"%s\"",
                                                    self->uuid,
                                                    self->name);
